{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.94,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "wrong_component_type",
      "components": ["U15", "U22", "U35", "U36"],
      "pins": ["U15.4", "U22.4", "U35.4", "U36.4"],
      "nets": ["ESTOP_OUT", "/ESTOP_SINK_ALL", "Net-(U15-Y)", "Net-(U15-A)"],
      "observed": "The e-stop buffers are named SN74LVC1G07QDCKTQ1, but their MPN fields specify U74LVC1G125G-AL5-R. The latter is a push-pull tri-state buffer, not the open-drain buffer type specified for the e-stop sink circuit.",
      "expected": "The e-stop sink outputs should use the specified open-drain buffer type, or another part with equivalent open-drain behavior. The specification describes U15, U22, U35 and U36 as SN74LVC1G07 buffers wired as e-stop sinks.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"U15\") (value \"SN74LVC1G07QDCKTQ1\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(field (name \"MPN\") \"U74LVC1G125G-AL5-R\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "single non-inverting buffers (`SN74LVC1G07`, parts `U15`, `U22`, `U35`, `U36`) wired as `/OE`-controlled sinks"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If the MPN is what is procured or assembled, these outputs actively drive high as well as low instead of acting as open-drain sinks. That can defeat the intended wired sink behavior and compromise e-stop signaling.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["U4", "U23"],
      "pins": ["U4.5", "U23.5"],
      "nets": ["unconnected-(U4-VP-Pad5)", "unconnected-(U23-VP-Pad5)"],
      "observed": "Both Ethernet protection arrays have their VP pins explicitly unconnected; their VN pins are connected to GND.",
      "expected": "For the specified TPD4E1U06 protection arrays, the positive clamp/reference pin should be connected as required by the protection circuit, rather than left floating.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"unconnected-(U4-VP-Pad5)\") (node (ref \"U4\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"VP\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"unconnected-(U23-VP-Pad5)\") (node (ref \"U23\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"VP\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"U4\") (value \"TPD4E1U06DCKR\")"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The arrays' positive-side steering/clamp path may not provide the intended Ethernet-line ESD protection, increasing the chance of damage or disruption from transients.",
      "confidence": 0.86
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files show a likely e-stop buffer sourcing mismatch: the listed MPN is a push-pull tri-state part while the specification requires open-drain sink buffers. They also leave the positive reference pins of both Ethernet ESD arrays unconnected, likely reducing their protection."
}

